course: dictionary
lesson: 6626
title: Nothing in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Nothing is a small word with a big job. Most often it means not anything at all: «There is nothing in the box.» Read the words around it to find which meaning fits, because the same word can mean different things.
explain: Context shows you the meaning. «Five take away five leaves nothing» means zero, no amount left. «A planetary nebula has nothing to do with planets» means the two things are not connected. «On a cloudy day it tells nothing at all» means the sundial gives no clue about the time.
explain: Nothing can also mean free: «for nothing» means without paying. In Dhruv's story, his dad «says nothing all evening» means he stays silent, not that he has gone away. Always test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: does it still make sense?
fact: Nothing means not anything at all, or zero.
fact: «For nothing» means free, or with no result.
fact: «Nothing to do with» means not connected to.
fact: «Nothing» in the penguin sentence means the fathers eat no food for about two months.
fact: The word «nothing» can also be a noun, but this use is rare, so most of the time it is a pronoun.
exercise: «There is nothing in the box.» What does nothing mean here? | Something heavy and hidden | A large empty room | Everything, all of it together | *Not anything at all
exercise: «Five take away five leaves nothing.» What does nothing mean here? | The first number you see | A shape with four sides | A very large number | *Zero, no amount left
exercise: «A planetary nebula has nothing to do with planets.» What does this mean? | It is the biggest planet in the sky | It is made of planets | *It is not connected to planets | It has planets all around it
test: «On a cloudy day it tells nothing at all.» What does nothing at all mean here? | *It gives no information at all | It shows the time exactly | It tells the time an hour late | It tells you the date
test: Nadia says, «I got these tickets for nothing.» What does for nothing mean? | Given back to the shop | With a very big price | *For free, without paying | Lost forever
exam: Dhruv's dad «says nothing all evening.» What does says nothing mean? | Tells a long and funny story | Says the same thing over and over | *Stays silent and says no words | Shouts loudly all evening
